    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-2209",
      "problem": "What number is missing from the division problem below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/0b119e18348ad6f0ee31f2ad3e57cad4fc66403302df5590a8526ce39e930c78.png)",
      "worked_solution": "We have $\\dfrac{3}{4}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{3}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/eb114471d69ebd728a176b521ab410ab2b16d2bccc039e003faacd9c5d445e96.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $\\color{blue}5$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $\\color{blue}5$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 3 4 \\div {\\color{blue}{5}} = \\dfrac{3}{20}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}5.$",
